; Commodity declarations - these set amount display styles and provide extra error checking.
; https://hledger.org/hledger.html#commodity-directive
; https://hledger.org/hledger.html#strict-checks

; Fiat currencies

commodity $1000.00
commodity 1000.00 EUR
;commodity 1 000 000,00 EUR   ; https://hledger.org/hledger.html#commodity-display-style can be customised

; Investment commodities
; Note commodity declarations must have a decimal mark (a period or comma), 
; even if no decimal digits follow it.

commodity 1. AAPL  ; lots:

; Cryptocurrencies

commodity 1.000000 ADA    ; lots:
commodity 1.00000000 BTC  ; lots:
commodity 1.00000000 ETH  ; lots:

; Other

; D declares a default commodity (and display style) to apply to bare numbers.
; This one can be useful if you include timedot files: it adds the h (hour)
; symbol, which is also the one used by timeclock files. 
;D 1.0h
